{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ANALYSIS (orchestrator-delegated critical evaluation):\n\n## Premise validation — VALID, with three minor factual errors\n\nIndependently verified against the working tree, git history, and the ticket store (2026-08-21):\n\n**Prior-art claims — all TRUE.** `docs/experiments/escaped-bug-review-gap-analysis.md` exists; line 66-67 is Class 3 with `halfwhite-chordal-stonefly` (\"--class requirement added to CLI, not to MCP transition_ticket + NDJSON import — 9 prior PASS reviews\"); that bug exists, closed `regression`, title matches. Lines 87-92 recommend exactly the three criteria named. `import-integrity` and `ci-gate-compat` appear NOWHERE in `src/` or `.rebar/` — never built (grep confirmed). `surface-parity` shipped narrower than the written recommendation: the rec says *content-triggered* + \"require the MCP tool + NDJSON/import path be updated in lockstep\"; the shipped overlay (`src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json`) is GLOB-triggered on exactly `**/_commands/**`, `**/_lib_writes.py`, `**/_mcp_writes.py`, `default_posture: advisory`, `blocking_enabled: false`, and its prompt (`code-review-surface-parity.md:19-21`) confines siblings to the lib/CLI/MCP triple — no NDJSON/import channel. `deletion-impact` verified content-triggered, blocking@0.60.\n\n**Coverage-gap claims — all TRUE.** T13's trigger is prohibition-only (\"apply only when the plan NEWLY FORBIDS a previously-permitted action\", `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md:322-325`). `omits_required_site` is a divergence *grade* on an axis, not a finder (guide lines 233, 243). Plan criteria count = 49 (confirmed via `registry.load_criteria()`). No criterion hunts additive-obligation misses; the residual-gap statement holds.\n\n**Over-fire data — TRUE.** `docs/plan-review-gate.md` (¶ at ~line 263): 18,085 plan-v3 verified findings; the 1,307-finding omitted-scope-site class graded `none` ~90% (1,173); a blunt widening would have flipped 4.3% of runs PASS→BLOCK. The ticket cites its own strongest counter-evidence honestly.\n\n**Commit claims — structurally TRUE.** `9844f6de35` touches `close_precheck.py` (+164) / `transition_close.py` (+29) and no `gates.py`, and updates BOTH `_commands/transition.py` and `_cli/help/transition.txt`. `0f999860ad` touches `_commands/transition.py` and NOT the help txt. `d575600381` touches exactly the three spawn files + new `_proc.py`. `57114212cf` is 2026-06-12. All three named commits glob-match surface-parity's `**/_commands/**` today, and the prompt's triple-scoping confirms it would still scope out the actual missed siblings.\n\n**Spot-checked evidence tickets — all real, statuses match:** `kaolinite-head-wildebeest` closed `not_a_bug` (the rejection discipline is genuine), `citric-preregal-ladybird` closed `regression` (external tests / 4 CI lanes), `cardinal-secluded-avocet` closed (REBAR_LLM_TIMEOUT), `chanceful-microbial-fallowdeer` closed `preexisting`.\n\n**Errors found (none undermines the conclusion):**\n1. \"14 code-review overlays\" — the registry has **15** `OVERLAY_IDS`.\n2. `9844f6de35` is dated **2026-08-14** in git, not 2026-08-15 as listed.\n3. \"the *earlier* `9844f6de35` updated both help sources, proving the pair was maintained before it drifted\" — chronology is BACKWARDS: `0f999860ad` (2026-07-19) predates `9844f6de35` (2026-08-14). The pair discipline was demonstrated *after* the drift, not before; the drift instance itself still stands.\n\n**Currency:** concurrent ticket d890-e711 (`legalistic-combustive-nymph`, open) normalizes two criteria *synonyms* (sec/documentation) — orthogonal to this proposal; no conflict. The audit here reflects the current criteria set.\n\n## Critical evaluation\n\n**Cost.** Gate-economics (rebar metrics, last 30d): cost_per_accepted_change ≈ 70.2, first_pass_verification ≈ 0.79. Every added criterion runs on matching reviews; a blocking one adds false-block risk on top. The project's own 90%-`none` data predicts a broad additive-obligation criterion would be dominated by immaterial findings — the ticket correctly rejects the broad form. P0 costs nothing at review time (it is decision/doc hygiene). P1/P2 are edits to *existing* overlays, not new review passes. P3 is the only proposal that adds a new pass, and the ticket itself gates it on residue.\n\n**Overlap.** Verified none: nearest mechanisms are a grader (`omits_required_site`), a wrong-trigger scan (T13, prohibitions), the subtractive mirror (`deletion-impact`), and a triple-scoped advisory (`surface-parity`). The gap is real.\n\n**Enforcement mechanics.** P3's four-element anti-fire threshold ((a) cited added line, (b) path:line of a discharging site in the same diff, (c) path:line of a non-discharging site, (d) observable consequence) is concrete and mirrors `project.portability`'s pattern (verified: blocking@0.9 in `.rebar/criteria_routing.json`). Caveat: \"obligation\" is inherently fuzzier than \"deleted def\" — deletion-impact earned blocking@0.60 on validity ≥0.95 for a *syntactic* trigger; an additive criterion should be expected to calibrate lower-precision, so advisory-first is right.\n\n**Failure modes.** Legit deliberate phased rollouts (e.g. `airy-starchy-muntjac` explicitly scoped MCP out) would fire; the MIGRATED/EXEMPTED/UNCOVERED triage + the shipped surface-parity's \"deliberately justified divergence must not fire\" clause handle this if carried over. Test-only \"missed sites\" (the kaolinite class) are excluded by element (d). The definition-sensitivity the ticket admits (24%→60% base rate depending on strictness) means the prompt MUST encode the strict three-clause form or precision collapses.\n\n## Recommendation: ADOPT-MODIFIED\n\nAdopt **P0, P1, P2** now; make **P3 explicitly conditional** on measured residue after P1/P2 (the ticket already says \"only if residue remains\" — the modification is to make that a hard sequencing gate, not an option), and hold ALL postures at **advisory** until the AC's calibration replay (≥5 origin commits, hit/miss recorded) and FP-ledger measurement complete. Also correct the three factual errors above in any doc that inherits this evidence.\n\nThree strongest reasons:\n1. **The residual gap is verified, not asserted.** T13 prohibition-only, deletion-impact subtractive, surface-parity advisory + triple-scoped + glob-triggered, omits_required_site a grade — each checked in the working tree today. No mechanism asks \"this change adds an obligation — enumerate the surfaces that owe it.\"\n2. **P0/P1 are already-justified debt, not new policy.** The repo's own gap analysis recommended three criteria off 43 measured regressions; two were never built and the third shipped narrower than written, omitting the channel from its founding bug. Closing or formally declining documented recommendations is the cheapest real progress and requires no new evidence.\n3. **The project's own calibration data bounds the risk.** The ~90%-`none` rate and the 4.3% PASS→BLOCK flip from blunt widening (18,085-finding corpus) are verified in docs/plan-review-gate.md — they simultaneously justify rejecting the broad criterion and demand the advisory-first, replay-gated posture for anything adopted.\n\n## Operator decisions beyond adopt/reject\n- P0 ruling direction: build `import-integrity`/`ci-gate-compat`, or write the decision-not-to into the gap-analysis doc (either satisfies the AC; someone must choose).\n- Blocking promotion for widened surface-parity: requires the calibration replay — who runs it and against what corpus (real LLM spend).\n- Whether P2's T13 lexicon widening (prohibition→obligation) risks diluting T13's current precision — a before/after replay on T13's own history would derisk it.\n- Sequencing with d890-e711: none required (orthogonal), but both touch criteria docs — coordinate doc edits to avoid churn."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787350320465743001,"uuid":"dd4a52db-ffc0-4ea1-8759-cc1485c87aca"}